{:id :EACL-FORMAL-068
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "public-id/list-vector-host-equality-before-custom-codec-resolution"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :false-grant
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before public identity boundary hardening"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "The assurance matrix modeled typed semantic object identity but omitted the unresolved public host-value boundary. Clojure equality can equate representation-distinct IDs that a deterministic injective custom codec resolves differently, allowing request-local batch memoization to reuse another object's decision and relationship mutation coalescing to discard an update. Public numeric deletion also shared an implicit native-EID fallback, and resolver failures could be treated as absence."
 :fix
 "Admit public batch memo keys only for canonical identity representations under the immutable/injective adapter contract; resolve relationship endpoints before coalescing; separate public object deletion from explicit native-EID deletion; propagate resolver failures; and add an authored Dafny identity-boundary model, public operation contracts, mutation controls, and cross-backend regressions."
 :closing-evidence
